# API

The API is a Hono app (`apps/api/src/app.ts`). Handlers create metadata, enqueue jobs, and return IDs. They do not run transcription, summarization, KB sync, hook generation, or FFmpeg.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
app.post('/api/recordings/:id/transcribe', async (c) => {
  const transcript = await speech.transcribe(input);
  return c.json(transcript);
});

// ✅ GOOD
app.post('/api/recordings', async (c) => {
  const recording = await createRecording(input);
  await queue.enqueue({ name: 'ingest-video', payload: { recordingId: recording.id } });
  return c.json({ id: recording.id }, 201);
});
```

## Route surface

- `POST/GET /api/recordings`, `GET/DELETE /api/recordings/:id`
- `GET /api/recordings/:id/transcript`, `GET /api/recordings/:id/transcript.vtt`
- `GET/POST /api/recordings/:id/summary`
- `POST /api/recordings/:id/add-to-global-kb`
- `GET /api/recordings/:id/hooks`, `POST /api/recordings/:id/hooks/generate`
- `GET/POST /api/knowledge-bases`
- `POST /api/clips`, `GET /api/clips/:id`

Wire providers at the composition root. Do not import PyAI or vendor SDKs in routes, controllers, or services.
